        "root_concepts": "[shear, strength]",
        "section": "geotechnical-engineering",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Shear Strength: Mohr-Coulomb, Triaxial Tests, Critical State, Residual Strength",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "1. **Mineral friction**: Quartz-quartz contact friction ≈ 26–30°\n2. **Particle interlocking**: denser/rounder particles → lower effective φ'\n3. **Dilation**: dense sands dilate (expand) during shear → extra resistance → φ'peak > φ'critical"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-SHEAR-STRENGTH.md#015",
      "path": [
        "04-SHEAR-STRENGTH.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
