        "root_concepts": "[shear, strength]",
        "section": "geotechnical-engineering",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Shear Strength: Mohr-Coulomb, Triaxial Tests, Critical State, Residual Strength",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "For design, distinguish:\n| Parameter | Meaning | Use |\n|-----------|---------|-----|\n| φ'peak | Strength at failure | Short-term, pre-failure calculations |\n| φ'critical state (φ'cv) | Strength after large strain (dilation complete) | Post-failure, residual |\n| φ'residual | Strength after very large strain (clay particles aligned) | Reactivated landslides |"
    }
